Two fixes; one corrects a wrong diagnosis I committed in 0cf0c70.

1. Codex P2 (valid, verified before accepting): tabs reorder live, so releasing
   outside every strip committed the preview. Old code only moved on a valid
   drop. Verified by probe: drag tab0 over tab2 previews
   [Projects,Settings,New work], release over the content area kept it instead
   of reverting. Fix: treat dragend with null target like Escape. Checked first
   that successful drops always carry a non-null target (tab drops report the
   tab sortable, strip drops report the strip droppable), so this cannot
   swallow real drops.

2. The CI-only Frontend failure was NOT what 0cf0c70 claimed. That commit added
   a dragend fallback for appendedToStripSpace, but the fallback reads
   event.operation.target, which is equally stale when collision detection never
   ran for the final position. CI still failed on 0cf0c70 with an identical
   trace. The fallback is idempotent and harmless so it stays, but it was never
   the fix.

   Real cause: Playwright dispatches mouse.move steps back to back and the
   helper called mouse.up() immediately after, so on a slow runner zero frames
   elapsed and dnd-kit's frame-driven collision pass never ran at the final
   position. Fixed by awaiting two requestAnimationFrames before release. A real
   pointer interleaves moves with frames, so this is not a magic sleep.

